=== Episode 9: Pâtisserie (Semi-final) ===
In the [[pâtisserie]] semifinal signature challenge, the bakers were tasked to make 24 dipped [[Madeleine (cake)|Madeleines]], in 2 designs and flavours, in {{frac|1|1|2}} hours. For the technical challenge, the bakers tackled Prue Leith's complex recipe for [[Torta setteveli|Torta Setteveli]], a 7-layered cake containing 2 light chocolate [[genoise]] sponges, hazelnut [[Bavarian cream|bavarois]], crunchy [[Praline (nut confection)|praline]] base and a chocolate [[mousse]], topped with a chocolate mirror glaze, to be completed in {{frac|3|1|2}} hours. For the penultimate showstopper challenge, the bakers were tasked to create a Parisian [[pâtisserie]] window containing 36 pâtisserie in 3 types: [[choux pastry]], {{lang|fr|italic=no|[[shortcrust pastry|pate sucree]]}} and [[puff pastry]] [[mille-feuille]], in 5 hours.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/live/2018/oct/23/great-british-bake-off-2018-semi-final-live |title =The Great British Bake Off 2018: semi-final - as it happened|date=23 October 2018|work=Guardian|accessdate=1 November 2018}}</ref>{{sticky header}}{{table alignment}}
