=== Episode 10: Final ===
For the final signature challenge, the last 3 bakers were required to make 12 iced [[doughnuts]] of 2 types, filled and ring, in 3 hours. The technical challenge was another Bake Off first, where the bakers were asked to carry out the challenge outside the tent. Using Paul Hollywood's recipe, the bakers needed to produce 6 [[pita]] breads in 90 minutes, to be served with 3 different dips: [[baba ghanoush]], smoked garlic [[salsa verde]] and burnt pepper salsa, using the open campfire set up outside. For the final showstopper, the bakers were asked to create an incredible landscape dessert with at least 3 different elements within it, in {{frac|4|1|2}} hours. During the showstopper, one of Rahul's storage glass jars exploded under the intense heat, which resulted in shards of broken glass shattered all over his bench and potentially contaminated his bakes, requiring clean up from the production team. As a result, he was given an extra 15 minutes for the challenge.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/live/2018/oct/30/the-great-british-bake-off-2018-final-find-out-who-takes-the-crown |title =The Great British Bake Off 2018: final - as it happened|date=30 October 2018|work=Guardian|accessdate=1 November 2018}}</ref>{{sticky header}}{{table alignment}}
